                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "background": 1,
                                                    "id": "obj-40",
                                                    "linecount": 9,
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 560.0, 300.0, 213.0, 136.0 ],
                                                    "text": "The Modulation LFO ramp passes through a pair of cycle~ objects, which contain a cosine waveform. By shifting the phase of the right channel, we obtain level and phase variations of both audio channels that permit to simulate a rotation of the sound in the stereo field, thanks to the MS matrix previously described."
                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "background": 1,
                                                    "id": "obj-39",
                                                    "linecount": 17,
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 560.0, 40.0, 223.0, 251.0 ],
                                                    "text": "The incoming stereo signals are converted to MS (mid-side) signals: the Left signal is the sum of L & R input signals (mono mix), and the Right signal is made of the difference of L & R input signals (i.e. combine the two channels with Right channel phase inverted). This provides signals similar to those produced by a mid-side microphone, where the mono capsule would include everything, with center-panned elements dominating, while the Side stereo capsule would contain only audio that’s different in the left and right channels. The audio result is an accurate stereo imaging, which can then be manipulated."
                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "background": 1,
                                                    "fontsize": 10.0,
                                                    "id": "obj-45",
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 345.5, 368.0, 63.0, 18.0 ],
                                                    "text": "Cos2 modul."
                                                }
                                            },
