                                        }
                                    },
                                    "text": "Double-click to see the embedded patches",
                                    "textjustification": 1
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-74",
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 280.0, 177.0, 77.0, 21.0 ],
                                    "text": "External LFO"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 0,
                                    "id": "obj-32",
                                    "linecount": 4,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 570.0, 390.0, 210.0, 64.0 ],
                                    "text": "The amount of amplitude modulation is controlled by the Depth parameter, which adjusts the mixing of the input with the processed signals. "
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 0,
                                    "id": "obj-27",
                                    "linecount": 5,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 570.0, 460.0, 196.0, 78.0 ],
                                    "text": "Also notice the +3 dB boost added to the processed signals, needed to compensate for some energy loss perceived through the amplitude modulation process."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 0,
                                    "id": "obj-26",
                                    "linecount": 7,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 570.0, 280.0, 220.0, 107.0 ],
                                    "text": "To obtain stereo modulation, we’re shifting the input phase of the cycle~ object whose waveform is used to control the amplitude of the right audio channel. The phase offset between L and R modulation waveforms is controlled by the Spread parameter."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 0,
                                    "id": "obj-25",
                                    "linecount": 3,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 570.0, 220.0, 210.0, 50.0 ],
                                    "text": "The cosine waveform is then used to increase and decrease the amount of amplitude applied to the input signal. "
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 0,
                                    "id": "obj-95",
                                    "linecount": 7,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 570.0, 110.0, 221.0, 107.0 ],
                                    "text": "The phasor~ object inside the LFO~ subpatcher generates a signal ramp, at a rate controlled by the Rate parameter. The rate can be set by tempo tapping. The ramp is used as a phase value (x) to read in a cosine wavetable stored in the cycle~ object (y). "
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 0,
                                    "fontname": "Lato Bold",
                                    "fontsize": 18.0,
                                    "id": "obj-96",
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 570.0, 35.0, 134.0, 28.0 ],
                                    "text": "RNBO ︎︎︎Tremolo"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
