                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-93",
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 770.0, 500.0, 171.0, 21.0 ],
                                    "text": "Allpass filters in Gen container"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 0,
                                    "fontname": "Lato Bold",
                                    "fontsize": 18.0,
                                    "id": "obj-96",
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 770.0, 35.0, 119.0, 28.0 ],
                                    "text": "RNBO Phaser"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-111",
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 770.0, 60.0, 167.0, 21.0 ],
                                    "text": "Classic stereo phaser effect"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-95",
                                    "linecount": 3,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 770.0, 430.0, 218.0, 50.0 ],
                                    "text": "Finally input and modulated signals are  mixed (added) together to obtain the phasing effect."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-92",
                                    "linecount": 16,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 770.0, 520.0, 220.0, 237.0 ],
                                    "text": "To enhance the phasing effect, the filtered signal is fed back into the filter bank, while the amount of feedback is dynamically controlled by the Depth parameter. In order to make a feedback loop possible in a patcher, we've embedded the filter bank in a Gen container. This wouldn't be possible in pure Rnbo, which is sample vector-based - we'd need to add a delay of at least one vector in order to make a feedback loop in the patcher, which would lead to less efficiency in the audio rendering. Additionally, Gen allows for creating one's own filter design in patching or dsp code forms."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-112",
                                    "linecount": 6,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 770.0, 330.0, 250.0, 93.0 ],
                                    "text": "To obtain stereo modulation, we’re shifting the input phase of the triangle~ object whose waveform is used to control the phasing of the right audio channel. The phase offset between L and R modulation waveforms is controlled by the Spread parameter."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-113",
                                    "linecount": 7,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 770.0, 220.0, 238.0, 107.0 ],
                                    "text": "The triangular waveform is then used to smoothly sweep across a frequency range, whose amplitude is defined by the Depth parameter, and whose central axis is defined by the Tone parameter. The frequency sweep is then applied to a cascade of four allpass filters."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-117",
                                    "linecount": 7,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 770.0, 110.0, 221.0, 107.0 ],
                                    "text": "The phasor~ object inside the LFO~ subpatcher generates a signal ramp, at a rate controlled by the Rate parameter. The rate can be set by tempo tapping. The ramp is used as a phase value (x) to read in a triangular wavetable stored in the triangle~ object (y). "
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-110",
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 300.0, 540.0, 21.0, 21.0 ],
                                    "text": "R"
                                }
                            },
